From: accel-virt
Subject: [PATCH] output merger logic ops are reported for every colour target format when the device has logic ops, not only the unsigned integer ones

accel-virt: logic ops apply to normalized and signed integer targets as well, and D3D12 refuses a pipeline whose logic op target format lacks the bit, so a UNORM target could not use the logic op the device offers.
---
--- a/libs/vkd3d/device.c
+++ b/libs/vkd3d/device.c
@@ -5235,7 +5235,7 @@
         {
             data->Support1 |= D3D12_FORMAT_SUPPORT1_RENDER_TARGET | D3D12_FORMAT_SUPPORT1_MULTISAMPLE_RENDERTARGET;
 
-            if (device->device_info.features2.features.logicOp && format->type == VKD3D_FORMAT_TYPE_UINT)
+            if (device->device_info.features2.features.logicOp)
                 data->Support2 |= D3D12_FORMAT_SUPPORT2_OUTPUT_MERGER_LOGIC_OP;
 
             /* This bit seems to only indicate support for AVERAGE resolves and is
